Scope and limitations:
Repartition of a previously used local NIH cohort, not a new blind cohort or official benchmark split.
Patient independence applies to the NEW adaptation splits, not prior studies or backbone pretraining.
Single-site 14-label evaluation; does not expand the small CheXpert cohort or establish cross-institution generalization.
Exact pixel duplicates checked; semantic/near-duplicate equivalence is not exhaustively audited.
Paired group resampling of fixed checkpoints; average per-seed metrics, not predictions. No training-cohort uncertainty or multiplicity adjustment. A missing class invalidates the entire macro draw; intervals conditional on full class presence when invalid draws occur.
The global CLS route replaces native disease aggregation; its difference from Pre is not a pure insertion-point effect.
All methods used the fixed prior protocol; no claim that each baseline is optimally tuned.
Hernia has 11 positive TEST images from 9 patients; per-class support and bootstrap validity are retained.
